    {
      "card_id": "card_46_electric_power_intro",
      "card_slug": "card_46_electric_power_intro",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "electric_power",
      "level": 6,
      "progress": {
        "current": 46,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Raju, bulb pe likha hota hai 60W, 100W. Ye W kya hai?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Watt Sir! Power ki unit!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Bilkul sahi! ELECTRIC POWER = Rate of doing work or rate of consumption of electrical energy. Matlab kitni energy kitne time mein consume ho rahi hai. Formula: P = W/t = VI = I²R = V²/R. Unit: WATT (W)!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Itne saare formulas?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_47_power_formulas",
        "button_text": "Formulas Samjho ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_47_power_formulas",
      "card_slug": "card_47_power_formulas",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "power_formulas",
      "level": 6,
      "progress": {
        "current": 47,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Sab connected hain! P = VI (basic definition). Ohm's law se V=IR, toh P = (IR)×I = I²R. Ya I=V/R, toh P = V×(V/R) = V²/R. Situation ke hisaab se use karo! ⭐ NEET/SSC Formula Favorite - Sabse zyada questions yahi se!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "1 Watt matlab?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "1 Watt = 1 Joule/second. Agar 1 Volt ki voltage se 1 Ampere current flow ho toh power = 1 Watt. Named after James Watt (Scottish inventor, improved steam engine). Larger unit: kilowatt (kW) = 1000 W!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Toh 100W bulb matlab 100 Joule per second energy consume karta hai?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_48_power_practical",
        "button_text": "Practical Use ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_48_power_practical",
      "card_slug": "card_48_power_practical",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "power_practical",
      "level": 6,
      "progress": {
        "current": 48,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Perfect! 100W bulb 220V pe chalaye toh current I = P/V = 100/220 = 0.45 A. Aur 10W LED bulb sirf 10/220 = 0.045 A kheenchega - 10 times less! Isliye LED energy efficient hai. Power rating appliances pe hota hai - fan 75W, TV 150W, AC 1500W!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "AC 1500W matlab bahut zyada current?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Haan! 1500/220 ≈ 7 Ampere! Isliye AC ke liye alag thicker wiring hoti hai. ⭐ BPSC TRE Domestic Application: High-power devices need thicker wires (less resistance, less heating, safe current carrying capacity!)"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Bijli ka bill kaise calculate hota hai Sir?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_49_energy_consumption",
        "button_text": "Energy Units ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_49_energy_consumption",
      "card_slug": "card_49_energy_consumption",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "energy_consumption",
      "level": 6,
      "progress": {
        "current": 49,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Brilliant question! Energy consumed = Power × Time. But commercial unit Joule nahi hai - wo bahut chhota hai. Commercial unit = kWh (kilowatt-hour) ya 'UNIT'. 1 kWh = energy consumed by 1 kW device running for 1 hour = 1000W × 3600s = 3.6 × 10⁶ Joules!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab bill mein Units likha hota hai?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Haan! Agar 100W bulb 10 hours chale toh energy = 100W × 10h = 1000 Wh = 1 kWh = 1 Unit. Agar rate ₹5 per unit hai toh cost = 1 × 5 = ₹5! ⭐ Railway/SSC Favorite Calculation Question!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Ye toh practical maths hai!"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_50_energy_example",
        "button_text": "Example Dekho ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_50_energy_example",
      "card_slug": "card_50_energy_example",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "energy_example",
      "level": 6,
      "progress": {
        "current": 50,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Example: Tumhare ghar mein 5 bulbs of 20W each, daily 5 hours chalte hain. 1 month (30 days) mein kitne units consume honge? Total power = 5×20 = 100W = 0.1kW. Time = 5h/day × 30 days = 150h. Energy = 0.1×150 = 15 kWh = 15 Units!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Agar rate ₹6 per unit ho toh bill = 15×6 = ₹90!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Perfect calculation! Isliye LED use karo - kam power, kam bill, energy saving! ⭐ UPSC/BPSC Energy Conservation & Environment Linkage Question! Electricity conservation = coal/fuel saving = less pollution!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Samajh gaya!"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_51_quiz_power_1",
        "button_text": "Test Karo ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_51_quiz_power_1",
