      },
      "quiz_payload": {
        "question": "Two bulbs of 40W and 60W are connected in series to a 220V supply. Which bulb will glow brighter?",
        "options": [
          { "id": "A", "text": "40W bulb" },
          { "id": "B", "text": "60W bulb" },
          { "id": "C", "text": "Both equally bright" },
          { "id": "D", "text": "Neither will glow" }
        ],
        "correct_option_id": "A",
        "explanation": "⭐ NEET/BPSC Tricky Question! In series, current is same through both. Power dissipated P = I²R. From P = V²/R, higher wattage bulb has LOWER resistance (60W has less R than 40W). Since same current flows, P=I²R means higher R bulb (40W) dissipates more power and glows brighter! Common trap - students think 60W always brighter."
      },
