      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Raju, tumhare ghar mein main switchboard se har room tak wiring kaise jati hai?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir wires hoti hain na walls ke andar!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Haan! Ye systematic hota hai - DOMESTIC ELECTRIC CIRCUIT. India mein supply 220V AC hoti hai (50 Hz frequency). Main supply meter se aati hai → MCB/Fuse box → har room ko parallel wiring mein distribute hoti hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Kitne tarah ki wires hoti hain?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_56_three_wire_system",
        "button_text": "Wire Types ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_56_three_wire_system",
      "card_slug": "card_56_three_wire_system",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "three_wire_system",
      "level": 7,
      "progress": {
        "current": 56,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Teen wires hoti hain: (1) LIVE WIRE (RED/BROWN color) - HIGH potential (+220V), current yahan se aata hai. (2) NEUTRAL WIRE (BLACK/BLUE) - ZERO potential, current return path. (3) EARTH WIRE (GREEN/YELLOW) - Safety wire, metal body se connected, leakage current ko ground mein bhej deta hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Earth wire kaise protect karta hai?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Agar kisi fault ki wajah se live wire appliance ke metal body ko touch kar jaye, toh without earth wire body 220V ho jayega - touch karo toh SHOCK! Earth wire body ko ground se connect karta hai (very low resistance path) - leakage current safely ground mein chala jata hai, aur fuse/MCB trip ho jata hai! ⭐ BPSC TRE Safety Concept!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab earth wire life saver hai!"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_57_earthing_importance",
        "button_text": "Earthing Detail ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_57_earthing_importance",
      "card_slug": "card_57_earthing_importance",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "earthing_importance",
      "level": 7,
      "progress": {
        "current": 57,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Absolutely! EARTHING/GROUNDING zaroori hai sabhi metal-body appliances ke liye - fridge, washing machine, AC, water heater. Three-pin plug mein bada pin earth wire ke liye hota hai. Two-pin plugs (phone charger) mein earth nahi kyunki plastic body hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir short circuit kya hota hai?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Jab live aur neutral wire directly touch kar jate hain (without load/resistance), toh current bahut zyada (almost infinite!) ho jata hai - ye SHORT CIRCUIT hai! I = V/R, agar R→0 toh I→∞! Isse bahut heat, sparks, fire ho sakti hai. Fuse/MCB turant melt/trip hokar circuit break karta hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Toh overloading kya hai?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_58_overloading",
        "button_text": "Overloading Samjho ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_58_overloading",
      "card_slug": "card_58_overloading",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "overloading",
      "level": 7,
      "progress": {
        "current": 58,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "OVERLOADING = Jab ek single socket mein bahut saare appliances connect kar do (multi-plug extension use karke). Total current = sum of individual currents. Agar wire ki safe current limit cross ho jaye (wire heat hone lage), toh overloading! Example: 5A wire pe 10A ka load!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Ye dangerous hai na?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Bahut! Wire heat → insulation melt → short circuit → fire! ⭐ BPSC/SSC Safety Rules: (1) Don't overload sockets, (2) Use proper rating wires, (3) MCB/Fuse mandatory, (4) Earth connection zaroori, (5) Don't touch switches with wet hands (water conducts current - shock!)"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Safety bahut important hai electricity mein!"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_59_safety_measures",
        "button_text": "Safety Measures ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_59_safety_measures",
      "card_slug": "card_59_safety_measures",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "safety_measures",
      "level": 7,
      "progress": {
        "current": 59,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Complete safety checklist: (1) ISI marked wires/switches use karo, (2) Proper earthing, (3) MCB rating according to load, (4) Don't use damaged wires/plugs, (5) Keep electrical items away from water, (6) Don't insert metal objects in sockets, (7) Main switch OFF karo before repair!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Agar kisi ko current lag jaye toh kya karein?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "PEHLE main switch OFF karo! Person ko directly touch mat karo (tumhe bhi shock lagega). Wooden stick ya dry cloth se push karke person ko wire se alag karo. Then medical help! ⭐ UPSC/BPSC First-Aid Knowledge!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Ye sab life-saving information hai Sir!"
        }
      ],
